<section id="about">
  <p class="about-intro">
    Self-taught. Background in advertising, then six years in product teams.
    Based in Bucharest. I got good at the React thing and then got bored
    of being good at the React thing — which is when the interesting problems started.
    Now I build tools, read specs and document the confusion honestly.
  </p>
  <div class="about-grid">
    <div class="about-block">
      <h3>What I do</h3>
      <p>Build web interfaces. Lately more interested in what the browser
      can do natively than what frameworks paper over. The distance between
      "technically works" and "makes someone feel something" is smaller than
      people assume, but you just have to care about both ends.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-block">
      <h3>How I think</h3>
      <p>Find something that shouldn't work and try it until it does. Read
      the spec, not just the tutorial. When something feels like magic,
      figure out what's underneath. Usually it's just something nobody
      bothered to check.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-block">
      <h3>What I reject</h3>
      <p>Generic advice. Frameworks that exist to justify their own
      complexity. Thought leadership with nothing to actually think about.
      Appearing certain as a career strategy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-block">
      <h3>What this version is</h3>
      <p>v0.1. A working title. The beta is real, not ironic.
      This site will change as I do. That's the point.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

